# nodes/console on its board, its console served on TCP port 4001.
#
# Renode holds the console's output until a client connects, then sends all of
# it, so the agent sees the node boot however late it attaches.

using sysbus
mach create "console"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl

# Renode's model of this board clocks the SysTick at 96 MHz, while Zephyr
# assumes the core's 480 MHz, so the node's time ran at 0.2x real time. At
# 480 MHz its log time stamps track virtual time to within 0.023%, and the node
# runs at 1.0000x real time.
sysbus.nvic Frequency 480000000

# Errors only, as in ../bench/renode-run.sh: Zephyr's D-cache maintenance writes
# registers Renode does not model, and each write logs a warning.
logLevel 3 nvic

# Also print the console to the container's log, for `just console`: the socket
# serves one client, and that is the agent.
showAnalyzer usart3

emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal 4001 "dut" false
connector Connect sysbus.usart3 dut

# Loaded from the reset macro, which Renode also runs when the firmware reboots.
macro reset "sysbus LoadELF @/elf/console.elf"
runMacro $reset

start
